        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f0082ccd-5469-5560-8169-e2820af92b77",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim McIlrath, Spike Slawson, Pete Wentz, Jay Jancetic, Daniel Binaei, Adam Bishop, Timothy Miller\n- Organizations: Arma Angelus, Rise Against, Fall Out Boy, Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, Uke-Hunt, Holy Roman Empire, Harm's Way, Racetraitor, Last Action Zeros, Mission Viejo High School, Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing\n- Places: Mission Viejo, California, Scottsdale, Arizona\n- Roles: punk rock musician, vocals, bass guitar, guitar, drums, lead singer, bassist, backing vocalist, English teacher, owner\n\nFacts:\n- Tim McIlrath was born on November 3, 1978.\n- Tim McIlrath is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson has been a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.\n- Pete Wentz was a member of Arma Angelus as a vocalist and later became the bass guitarist and a backing vocalist in Fall Out Boy.\n- Tim McIlrath was a member of Arma Angelus as a bass guitarist and later became the lead singer of Rise Against.\n- Jay Jancetic was a member of Arma Angelus as a guitarist and later played guitar for Holy Roman Empire and Harm's Way.\n- Daniel Binaei was a member of Arma Angelus as a guitarist and was formerly in Racetraitor.\n- Adam Bishop was a member of Arma Angelus as a guitarist and later became an English teacher at Mission Viejo High School in Mission Viejo, California.\n- Timothy Miller was a member of Arma Angelus as a drummer, later played drums for Last Action Zeros, and became the owner of Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing in Scottsdale, Arizona.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
